                <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-gray-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="p-6 md:p-8 bg-gray-50 border-t border-gray-100 prose max-w-none text-gray-700">
                <p>National Hearings Committee ruled in January that all ten national Board members who participated in the September motion were to be dismissed from their roles, and prohibited from holding any further Mensa office for several further years. Jay Friedlander of GLAAM was appointed as the non-voting &#39;Regional Coordinator&#39; pending further action.</p>
<p>Anrey Wang appointed on February 1 to succeed Jonathan Elliott as Webmaster.</p>
<p>Third consecutive Regional Gathering at the Golden Sails Hotel in Long Beach, from February 14-16, once again chaired by Jay Friedlander and Madeline Walker. This time we made $2300 on the event.</p>
<p>Jonathan Elliott retired as Chair of the Awards Committee following some twenty years, succeeded by Jana Bickel. David Fenig retired as Chair of the Elections Committee after thirteen years.</p>
<p>National Mensa Chair Lori Norris was recalled by a vote of the national Mensa membership, with the ballots counted and the results announced at the Annual Gathering held during July in Chicago.</p>
<p>A petition brought by the ten dismissed members of the national board, seeking reinstatement in their roles, was dismissed by the New York civil court in August.</p>
<p>Jay Friedlander was declared elected as Regional Vice Chair in November.</p>

            </div>
